   "narrative": "By June an outbreak was reported in China, and in July the Ottoman army recorded its first cases. The first wave had disrupted the war more than it had killed: three-quarters of the French troops, half the British forces and over 900,000 German soldiers fell sick. In the United States about 75,000 influenza deaths were reported in the first half of 1918, against some 63,000 in the same months of 1915. Through July the wave receded.",
