   "id": "october",
   "title": "October 1918, the deadliest month",
   "time": "October 1918",
   "narrative": "October 1918 was the worst month of the whole pandemic. The United States reported about 292,000 deaths between September and December; a war-bond parade in Philadelphia on 28 September was followed by an outbreak that killed some 12,000. Bombay counted about 15,000 dead out of 1.1 million, and India as a whole lost at least 12 million people. South Africa lost about 300,000 in six weeks, among them almost a quarter of the diamond-mine workforce of Kimberley. The wave swept across Russia and reached China, Japan and Brazil.",
