   "narrative": "In January 1919 death rates jumped again in most American cities, from New York to San Francisco, before falling from mid-February; nearly 160,000 Americans died of influenza and pneumonia in the first half of the year. England and Wales peaked in early March, France and the Netherlands in February, and Spain suffered a strong recurrence from January to April. Australia, shielded through 1918 by a strict maritime quarantine, saw its first epidemic in Melbourne in January, peaking in mid-February before spreading to New South Wales and South Australia. Madagascar had its first cases in April.",
